[00:13.94]1. Other sheep Jesus has, and they serve alongside
[00:20.58]those anointed to be Christ’s heavenly bride.
[00:29.04]All the things that are done
[00:31.76]for their comfort and aid
[00:35.80]Are things he considers that must be repaid.
[00:44.32](Chorus)
[00:44.32]“If you comforted them, you comforted me.
[00:53.58]If you did it for them, you did it for me.
[01:02.48]Your labors for them were your labors for me.
[01:11.70]You did it for them; you did it for me.
[01:19.94]If you did it for them, you did it for me.”
[01:31.87]2. “Yes, you comforted me in my hunger and thirst,
[01:38.67]and whatever my need, you came to me first.”
[01:46.73]“Tell us, when did we do this?”
[01:50.65]these ones will reply.
[01:54.07]The King will then answer them, telling them why:
[02:01.99](Chorus)
[02:02.37]“If you comforted them, you comforted me.
[02:11.17]If you did it for them, you did it for me.
[02:20.59]Your labors for them were your labors for me.
[02:29.87]You did it for them; you did it for me.
[02:38.05]If you did it for them, you did it for me.”
[02:49.58]3. “You’ve been loyal to me, doing works that are fine,
[02:56.82]as you preach alongside these brothers of mine.”
[03:05.26]So the King will then say
[03:08.44]to the sheep on his right:
[03:12.02]“Inherit the earth and perfection of life.”
[03:22.20](Chorus)
[03:22.20]“If you comforted them, you comforted me.
[03:32.36]If you did it for them, you did it for me.
[03:40.58]Your labors for them were your labors for me.
[03:49.66]You did it for them; you did it for me.
[03:57.86]If you did it for them, you did it for me.”
